WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.697
These are the key habits from Module 12.

00:00:02.697 --> 00:00:05.262
Treat important views as contracts.

00:00:05.262 --> 00:00:09.282
Separate stable reusable meaning from report-specific logic.

00:00:09.282 --> 00:00:11.527
Understand whether a view is writable.

00:00:11.527 --> 00:00:16.462
Be precise about the difference between limiting an interface and enforcing authorization.

00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:20.227
Remember that materialized views create a freshness obligation.

00:00:20.227 --> 00:00:23.667
And inspect dependencies before changing shared objects.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:28.947
Connect this idea to a governance project limiting which columns different users can access.

00:00:28.947 --> 00:00:33.582
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.582 --> 00:00:39.957
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:44.727
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:44.727 --> 00:00:49.680
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
